1
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:10,550
I'm sorry, did you just say it's Rachel?

2
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:13,630
Yes.

3
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:18,470
Um, you like Rachel?

4
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:23,640
Yes. I like Rachel.

5
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,360
Rachel?

6
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:35,950
Yeah. Okay, but look, you know...

7
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,490
You know who else I like? You.

8
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:42,490
And it doesn't get said enough. I like you, Ross.

9
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:47,210
"Rachel" Rachel?

10
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:47,210
It's not a big deal.

11
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,880
It's not a big deal? I'm sorry, I just...

12
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:54,340
What about the stuff you said?

13
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:59,260
How you can't stop thinking about her? How you can't sleep?

14
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:01,260
I'm an actor, you know?

15
00:01:01,510 --> 00:01:05,390
As a group, we tend to be overdramatic.

16
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:08,810
Rachel-who's-carrying-my-baby Rachel?

17
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:12,440
I know it's bad. And I know it's wrong, okay?

18
00:01:12,650 --> 00:01:15,780
It's not like anything's ever gonna happen.

19
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:18,990
These are just feelings. They'll go away.

20
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,740
You know, I gotta go.

21
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:23,290
Hey, Ross...

22
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,460
You know, I just have one... Rachel?

23
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:33,670
Rachel?

24
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:40,180
Rachel?

25
00:02:20,970 --> 00:02:23,890
Oh, oh! Okay, she's kicking.

26
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:27,350
She's growing inside you.

27
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:33,360
That was a big one.

28
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:33,360
That's the youngest girl to reject me.

29
00:02:34,270 --> 00:02:35,770
You guys!

30
00:02:34,270 --> 00:02:35,770
Hey there.

31
00:02:36,070 --> 00:02:39,280
Let me ask you. Do you believe in soul mates?

32
00:02:39,570 --> 00:02:40,780
Oh, yes, I do.

33
00:02:40,990 --> 00:02:43,780
There's one person out there for everyone.

34
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:46,990
You know how you find him? Stop looking.

35
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:50,250
I've stopped looking for Russell Crowe.

36
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,290
He'll find me.

37
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:53,630
Uh-huh. And you?

38
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:59,090
No. I believe that, uh, certain people are more suited for each other, but...

39
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,930
Soul mates? I don't think they exist.

40
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,930
Good.

41
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,930
Why?

42
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,930
Well, last night, I met Monica's.

43
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:11,020
What?

44
00:03:11,270 --> 00:03:15,150
I had a date with this guy. I swear he's her other half.

45
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:20,530
You don't think there's somebody better suited for Monica than me?

46
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,700
Well, what's he like?

47
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:29,330
He's tall. He has brown hair.

48
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:29,330
Of course.

49
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:34,000
A tall guy with hair similar to mine? Oh, unknowable universe!

50
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:37,250
He works with food.

51
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:37,250
Oh, sure. Older?

52
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,960
Obviously. And he's British.

53
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,960
I was just gonna ask!

54
00:03:40,170 --> 00:03:45,680
Yeah? And he's so centered, and mature and confident.

55
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:48,350
It's so sad they never met.

56
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:53,140
Luckily, the guy she settled for can't hear you.

57
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:56,150
Oh, I'm so sorry. Maybe I'm wrong.

58
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:59,320
We're going out again. I'll find out more.

59
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:02,490
He's meant for her, and you're gonna date him?

60
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:05,950
He may not be my soul mate, but a girl's gotta eat.

61
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,160
Hey.

62
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,160
Hey.

63
00:04:13,330 --> 00:04:16,580
I talked to Joey. I wanted to see you.

64
00:04:16,790 --> 00:04:20,880
I still can't believe it. Joey and Rachel?

65
00:04:21,090 --> 00:04:24,220
It's like you and me going out, only weirder.

66
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:27,300
I know you're hurting...

67
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:29,510
...but don't say that again.

68
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:35,440
What if they marry? He'd be the stepfather of my child.

69
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:37,770
You don't need to worry about.

70
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:40,480
He'll never tell her how he feels.

71
00:04:40,730 --> 00:04:43,610
If he did, you don't know how she'd react.

72
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:47,820
Sure, women never like Joey. I think he's a virgin.

73
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:52,830
He isn't thinking about going for her.

74
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:52,830
He's not?

75
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:56,750
All he's thinking about is how you're taking this.

76
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,920
It's freaking him out. He wants to move to Vermont.

77
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:05,470
Why?

78
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:05,470
He wants to leave the country.

79
00:05:10,050 --> 00:05:11,930
He thinks you hate him.

80
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:14,730
Hate him?

81
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:18,850
No, I don't hate him.

82
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:24,280
It's just, it's Rachel. You know?

83
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:28,610
I can't even imagine how hard this must be for you...

84
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:32,830
...but I don't want you to lose Joey over it.

85
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:37,460
Right now, he needs to know that you're still his friend.

86
00:05:38,830 --> 00:05:41,750
Okay, I'll talk to him.

87
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,670
I'd do it soon.

88
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:48,800
He just asked me how to convert his dollars into Vermont money.

89
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:57,140
Oh, hi!

90
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:57,140
Hi.

91
00:05:57,350 --> 00:06:00,600
Chandler, Monica, this is Don.

92
00:05:57,350 --> 00:06:00,600
Hello.

93
00:06:00,770 --> 00:06:02,770
Hello, nice to meet you.

94
00:06:00,770 --> 00:06:02,770
Nice to meet you.

95
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:04,780
Soul mate.

96
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:11,280
What are you guys doing?

97
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:11,280
We had lunch at Adriatica.

98
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:16,160
What's with the sun-dried tomatoes?

99
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:16,160
I know! Is this 1985?

100
00:06:16,370 --> 00:06:20,080
That's what I said! Isn't it strange?

101
00:06:16,370 --> 00:06:20,080
Not really.

102
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:23,960
What's wrong with sun-dried tomatoes?

103
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,670
On a barbecued-chicken pizza?

104
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,340
No?

105
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:35,390
What restaurants do you like?

106
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:35,390
Octavio. 27-and-7.

107
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:39,940
There's this place, Alessandro's.

108
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:39,940
Oh, my God! I'm the chef!

109
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:42,980
You're kidding! Your food is fantastic!

110
00:06:43,230 --> 00:06:47,320
I want to talk about your menu. Anyone want coffee?

111
00:06:47,530 --> 00:06:50,820
If you're talking about me, I'll go with you.

112
00:06:53,530 --> 00:06:55,200
What are you doing?

113
00:06:55,830 --> 00:06:59,200
I swear, I didn't know you guys would be here.

114
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:01,870
You don't believe in soul mates, so...

115
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:06,040
I believe in handsome strangers who hit on my wife.

116
00:07:06,250 --> 00:07:11,470
Just because I think they're soul mates doesn't mean anything'll happen.

117
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:14,010
Phoebe? Good work.

118
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:14,010
Yeah?

119
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:16,890
He's great. I love him.

120
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:22,520
Don't worry, we'll find you someone else.

121
00:07:31,530 --> 00:07:34,360
Hey.

122
00:07:31,530 --> 00:07:34,360
Hey.

123
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:39,370
I understand if you came by to hit me. I deserve it.

124
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:41,870
No, I don't want to hit you.

125
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:44,580
What, then? Kick me?

126
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:46,170
No.

127
00:07:47,130 --> 00:07:48,880
Bite me?

128
00:07:49,590 --> 00:07:52,130
I don't want to do anything to you.

129
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:55,590
I just want to say I'm not mad at you...

130
00:07:57,050 --> 00:08:00,390
...and that I certainly do not hate you.

131
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:04,190
I just came here to say that.

132
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:06,730
Hey, wait, Ross?

133
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:11,900
You wanna come in for a beer or something?

134
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,070
Yeah, sure.

135
00:08:19,910 --> 00:08:22,500
You got any beer?

136
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:28,590
All I got is melon stuff that Rachel left.

137
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,420
Okay.

138
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:41,180
You need to understand something.

139
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:49,440
I am never gonna act on this Rachel thing, okay?

140
00:08:49,690 --> 00:08:54,490
I wouldn't do anything to jeopardize my friendship with you.

141
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:57,320
Thank you.

142
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:18,180
Anyway, it'll just...

143
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:21,760
It'll take me a while to get over her.

144
00:09:22,010 --> 00:09:26,140
I'm not sure how to do that. I've never been in love, so...

145
00:09:26,390 --> 00:09:27,890
What?

146
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:33,020
You're in love with her?

147
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:37,990
Yeah. I thought you knew that.

148
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:37,990
Um, no.

149
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:44,290
Look, if it helps, I don't want to feel this way, honest.

150
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:48,870
I just keep thinking, "I'll get over this," you know?

151
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:53,040
But it just keeps getting harder.

152
00:09:53,250 --> 00:09:56,720
I don't know what to do, you know?

153
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,340
What do I do?

154
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:12,360
You need to tell her how you feel.

155
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:12,360
That's the green stuff talking.

156
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:17,860
I'm serious. You need to find out where she is.

157
00:10:18,110 --> 00:10:22,030
If she's not where you are, you can start to move on.

158
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:25,410
But what if, and I'm not saying she will be...

159
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:28,960
If she is where you are...

160
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:35,710
...then my feeling weird shouldn't stand in the way.

161
00:10:36,210 --> 00:10:38,800
Are you sure?

162
00:10:36,210 --> 00:10:38,800
Yeah.

163
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:42,930
If she ends up with somebody else...

164
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:47,060
...the truth is, she couldn't find a better guy.

165
00:10:47,810 --> 00:10:49,600
Hey, thanks.

166
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:56,190
So when are you gonna talk to her?

167
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:56,190
Oh, my God. I have to tell her.

168
00:10:57,320 --> 00:11:00,780
I haven't thought about it. What should I say?

169
00:11:00,990 --> 00:11:03,570
I'm understanding, but let's not get carried away.

170
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:06,990
Right, sorry. Sorry.

171
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,370
What am I gonna say?

172
00:11:13,250 --> 00:11:15,750
Yeah, tell me about it.

173
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:35,230
I'm phasing out the wine importing and focusing more on the, um, cheese.

174
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,360
Cheese, you say?

175
00:11:37,610 --> 00:11:40,940
That's some pretty smelly work, huh, Don?

176
00:11:41,530 --> 00:11:45,160
Excuse me?

177
00:11:41,530 --> 00:11:45,160
Cheese. It's smelly.

178
00:11:46,030 --> 00:11:49,540
You must smell a lot of the time too.

179
00:11:50,790 --> 00:11:55,960
Uh, not really. But with cheese, I think the smellier, the better.

180
00:11:56,170 --> 00:12:00,880
Me too! Chandler hates it. I can't have blue cheese in the house.

181
00:12:01,090 --> 00:12:04,180
And you're still married to him?

182
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:14,060
I would like to go to France and eat nothing but bread and cheese.

183
00:12:14,310 --> 00:12:16,560
Not even bread. Just cheese.

184
00:12:16,770 --> 00:12:18,690
No, I want the bread.

185
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:21,320
And pastries.

186
00:12:21,610 --> 00:12:23,650
And pate.

187
00:12:24,030 --> 00:12:27,700
I'm really not high. I just used to be fat.

188
00:12:28,490 --> 00:12:32,040
I have a villa in the Loire Valley you can stay in.

189
00:12:32,250 --> 00:12:34,370
Is it made of cheese?

190
00:12:37,330 --> 00:12:40,920
No. A house made of cheese, wouldn't that be great?

191
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:44,010
I'd move in tomorrow!

192
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:44,010
Oh, come on!

193
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,010
Listen to this!

194
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,010
I'm so sorry.

195
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:52,520
What do we do?

196
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:52,520
They both want a house of cheese.

197
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:56,100
I don't know how you fight that.

198
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:06,860
Okay, okay. I can do this. I can tell her how I feel.

199
00:13:07,110 --> 00:13:09,450
Okay, stand up straight.

200
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:12,580
Take a couple deep breaths.

201
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:16,080
Look confident.

202
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:21,920
Joey? What's up?

203
00:13:22,170 --> 00:13:26,550
I came by because I want to talk to you about something.

204
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:27,840
What's up?

205
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:31,220
Here, in the hall? What are we, animals?

206
00:13:31,430 --> 00:13:34,890
I'm late for a meeting. Could you make it quick?

207
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:38,730
I just came by to tell you that...

208
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:42,980
...I want to have dinner with you.

209
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:47,780
Sure. Just tell me where to meet you.

210
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:47,780
Okay.

211
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:51,280
Okay. That's good.

212
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:54,830
That gives you a couple of hours to prepare.

213
00:13:55,790 --> 00:13:58,370
Don't you people ever knock?

214
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:02,710
I'd like to have Don and Phoebe over.

215
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,380
Sure. Set it up.

216
00:14:04,590 --> 00:14:07,840
I'll just be browsing through the personals.

217
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:11,340
Are you okay? You're acting weird.

218
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,600
Yeah. Fine.

219
00:14:12,850 --> 00:14:14,180
Not perfect.

220
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:16,310
But good enough.

221
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:18,390
Jeez, what's with you?

222
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:21,650
I'm sorry, did you say "cheese"?

223
00:14:23,110 --> 00:14:27,320
What's going on?

224
00:14:23,110 --> 00:14:27,320
Phoebe says you and Don are soul mates.

225
00:14:27,530 --> 00:14:30,780
I don't believe in that, but you two get along.

226
00:14:31,030 --> 00:14:36,290
I'll step aside if you wanna go with Don and live in a house of cheese.

227
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:41,620
You don't believe in soul mates?

228
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:41,620
No, but I'm sure "tomatoes" does.

229
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:46,050
I don't believe in soul mates, either.

230
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,550
You don't?

231
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,550
Nope.

232
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:50,380
We weren't destined to end up together.

233
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:54,220
We fell in love and work hard at our relationship.

234
00:14:54,470 --> 00:14:57,140
Some days we work really hard.

235
00:14:57,770 --> 00:15:01,980
So you don't want to live with Don in a cheese house?

236
00:15:02,190 --> 00:15:08,190
No, I've had second thoughts. Do you know how hard it'd be to clean?

237
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,900
I love you.

238
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,900
I know.

239
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,660
I'm gonna take you out to dinner.

240
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:18,290
I found this place that makes the greatest mozzarella sticks and jalapeno poppers.

241
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,040
No? They taste so good.

242
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:31,840
It happens whenever Chandler touches my stomach.

243
00:15:32,050 --> 00:15:34,930
I'm worried the baby won't like him.

244
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:41,230
Are you okay?

245
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:41,230
Yeah, sure.

246
00:15:42,350 --> 00:15:46,730
Uh, look, the reason...

247
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:50,820
Is it hot in here?

248
00:15:51,030 --> 00:15:54,280
No, not for me. Why don't you take off your sweater?

249
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,240
This is a nice place...

250
00:15:57,490 --> 00:16:02,290
...and my T-shirt has a picture of Calvin doing Hobbes.

251
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:06,290
Oh, my God, really? Can I see it?

252
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:07,750
Yeah, sure.

253
00:16:10,590 --> 00:16:14,260
I wouldn't think Hobbes would like that so much.

254
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:22,390
How long have we known each other?

255
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:25,230
Um, seven, eight...

256
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:27,520
Eight years. Wow.

257
00:16:27,730 --> 00:16:29,820
Uh-huh. A long time.

258
00:16:27,730 --> 00:16:29,820
Yeah.

259
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:34,150
But over the past few weeks, I...

260
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:38,910
Okay! Sorry about the wait, but it is mega-jammed in here.

261
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,870
Our specials tonight...

262
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:43,750
Could you give us a second?

263
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:43,750
Sure.

264
00:16:43,910 --> 00:16:45,250
Second's up!

265
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:52,090
Not that kind of table.

266
00:16:55,430 --> 00:16:56,930
So you were saying?

267
00:16:58,850 --> 00:17:00,010
I'm not sure.

268
00:17:00,260 --> 00:17:04,980
